Levels: Gates

Purpose:
  Defines gate levels L0-L5 and default gate matrix.

Levels:
  L0: Prototype — minimal checks
  L1: Small project — basic test + lint
  L2: Production application — security + integration + deployment
  L3: Business-critical — performance + security + observability
  L4: High-scale — resilience + DR + advanced security
  L5: Mission-critical — formal controls + continuous verification

GateMatrix:
  | Gate            | L1 | L2 | L3 | L4 | L5 |
  | --------------- | -- | -- | -- | -- | -- |
  | Lint            | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | Unit            | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | Integration     | opt | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | E2E             | opt | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | SAST            | opt | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | DAST            | ❌ | opt | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | Pentest         | ❌ | risk | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | Load            | ❌ | risk | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
  | DDoS resilience | ❌ | ❌ | opt | ✅ | ✅ |
  | DR              | ❌ | opt | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |

QualityProfile:
  ProjectLevel: <L0-L5>
  BusinessCriticality: <LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH|CRITICAL>
  DataSensitivity: <LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH>
  InternetExposure: <YES|NO>
  Scale: <DAU/MAU/RPS>

Rules:
  [LV1] Gate selection is based on project level and context.
  [LV2] Default matrix may be overridden by project-specific policy.
  [LV3] Higher levels include all lower level gates.

